{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"216fe19cd2834b7bb4dcc34b37fa33c9968b47825d9bc71eff8057b06174977f","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconciliation differ and mutation filtering","key_entities":["compute_mutations","field_drift","unbound_local","_compute_mutations_emit_both","prev_snapshot","curr_snapshot","snapshot_head","mutation_count","test_key_set_prev_field_drift_never_survives_the_production_filter","test_a_genuinely_new_remote_key_still_plans_its_inbound_create","test_seed_mutations_survive_the_suppression","Gerrit 1256","6cdd4b00d9ee"],"problem_keywords":["verification","call-site suppression","differ contract","field drift","mutation filtering","no production change"],"propositions":["The raw differ compute_mutations API correctly emits field_drift as a positive control when local_state and jira_state differ, but the production snapshot call-site filter suppresses this emission by design.","A4-1 merges a deliberate call-site filter that prevents differ-owned emissions without modifying the pure differ contract, preserving the positive control for future local-state migrations.","The suppression filter at the production call site does not prevent genuine inbound-create mutations or invariant seed repairs from being processed.","Converged reconciliation passes record zero mutation_count and zero downstream git operations after the call-site filter is applied to snapshot comparisons."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787321924077073001,"uuid":"ad1b7f00-f79d-48bd-a7c1-1af987828451"}